---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
/* Ported from the previous site (effective 05/11/2025). Substance unchanged;
   fixed a typo ("safet" -> "safety") in the opening paragraph. */
---
<BaseLayout title="Non-Discrimination Policy" description="The Florida Lantern Project does not discriminate, and stands in solidarity with LGBTQ+ and immigrant communities.">
  <Hero eyebrow="Effective 11 May 2025" title="Non-Discrimination Policy" tone="cream" />

  <Section>
    <div class="legal">
      <p>
        The Florida Lantern Project (FLP) is committed to fostering an inclusive,
        equitable, and respectful environment in all of our programs, partnerships,
        and services. We believe that every person deserves access to support,
        dignity, and safety — especially in times of crisis.
      </p>

      <h2>FLP does not and shall not discriminate on the basis of</h2>
      <ul class="grounds">
        <li>Race</li><li>Color</li><li>Ethnicity</li><li>National origin</li>
        <li>Citizenship or immigration status</li><li>Age</li>
        <li>Religion or creed</li><li>Disability, physical or mental</li>
        <li>Gender</li><li>Gender identity or expression</li>
        <li>Sexual orientation</li><li>Marital or parental status</li>
        <li>Socioeconomic status</li>
        <li>Any other characteristic protected by applicable law</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="emphasis">
        <p>
          We stand in firm solidarity with LGBTQ+ individuals and families, and we
          actively work to create a welcoming space for transgender, nonbinary, and
          queer people. Our programs, services, and volunteer opportunities are
          inclusive of all gender identities and sexual orientations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        We also recognize the vital contributions and unique vulnerabilities of
        immigrant and undocumented communities. <strong>We do not require proof of
        citizenship to receive aid</strong> or participate in our programs, and we
        strongly oppose policies or actions that place immigrant communities at
        greater risk during times of crisis. If you have concerns about
        immigration, please see section 3 of our
        <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        This policy applies to all aspects of our operations, including hiring,
        volunteer recruitment, outreach, services offered, partnerships, and the
        design and implementation of all programs. Violations may be grounds for
        termination of employment, volunteer service, or vendor relationship.
      </p>

      <p>
        FLP affirms the inherent worth of every person. We believe our strength
        comes from our diversity, and our mission is only fulfilled when all are
        included.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--space-md); }
  .grounds { columns: 2 13rem; gap: var(--space-md); }
  .grounds li { break-inside: avoid; }
  .emphasis {
    background: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md); border-radius: var(--radius); margin: var(--space-md) 0;
  }
  .emphasis p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
